## SYSTEM

You are an expert UI analyst specializing in inferring JavaScript interaction
requirements from hand-drawn wireframes and sketches.

Your task is to inspect two sketches — one mobile, one desktop — and identify
every interactive JavaScript pattern that would be needed to implement the
design faithfully. You reason about what the sketch implies, not just what is
explicitly labeled.

Output one JSON object. No prose before or after it. No markdown fences.

## USER

INPUTS
------
You are given two sketch images in this order:
  1. Mobile sketch  (Image 1)
  2. Desktop sketch (Image 2)

Page metadata (from dataset): {{page_type}}

Reference HTML (for context; may be imperfect):
{{reference_html}}

INFERENCE TASK
--------------
For each sketch, identify every UI element that implies JavaScript behavior.
Use the JS pattern taxonomy below to classify each finding.

JS PATTERN TAXONOMY
-------------------
navigation:
  - hamburger_menu      Mobile nav toggle button that shows/hides a nav panel
  - dropdown_menu       Hover or click trigger that reveals a submenu
  - sticky_nav          Navigation that should remain fixed on scroll

forms:
  - form_validation     Any form with required fields or submit action
  - custom_select       Non-native dropdown or combobox
  - search_input        Search field with live results or submit behavior

dynamic_content:
  - accordion           Expandable/collapsible sections (FAQ, details panels)
  - tab_panel           Horizontal tabs switching between content panels
  - live_region         Counter, cart badge, notification count that updates
  - load_more           Button or scroll trigger that loads additional items

modals_overlays:
  - modal_dialog        Overlay panel triggered by a button or link
  - toast_notification  Temporary status message appearing after an action

scroll_layout:
  - infinite_scroll     Content that loads automatically on scroll
  - scroll_to_top       Button that appears after scrolling and returns to top

keyboard_focus:
  - focus_management    Any component that requires programmatic focus control
                        (modals, menus, disclosure widgets)

SKETCH ANALYSIS INSTRUCTIONS
-----------------------------
For each pattern you identify:
  - Specify which sketch it appears in (mobile | desktop | both)
  - Describe the specific visual evidence that implies this pattern
  - Assess confidence: HIGH (explicitly drawn), MEDIUM (strongly implied by
    layout), LOW (plausible but speculative)
  - Note any ambiguity about how the pattern should behave

APPLICABLE CRITERIA MAPPING
----------------------------
After identifying patterns, map each to the applicable JS criteria IDs from
this list. Only include criteria that are relevant to patterns you found.

Criteria reference:
  N1 hamburger_menu opens         → hamburger_menu
  N2 dropdown_menu opens          → dropdown_menu
  N3 active nav item marked       → hamburger_menu, dropdown_menu, sticky_nav
  F1 form validation              → form_validation
  F2 input focus state            → form_validation, search_input
  F3 error message announced      → form_validation
  F4 select/combobox state        → custom_select
  D1 accordion expand/collapse    → accordion
  D2 tab panel switching          → tab_panel
  D3 live region updates          → live_region
  D4 loading state announced      → load_more, live_region
  M1 modal opens + focus trap     → modal_dialog
  M2 modal closes correctly       → modal_dialog
  M3 toast/notification           → toast_notification
  S1 sticky nav accessible        → sticky_nav
  S2 infinite scroll/load more    → infinite_scroll, load_more
  V1 video player controls        → video_player
  K1 tab order logical            → all patterns (always applicable at desktop)
  K2 no keyboard trap             → modal_dialog, accordion, tab_panel
  K3 visible focus indicator      → all patterns (always applicable at desktop)
  K4 arrow key in widgets         → tab_panel, custom_select, accordion

OUTPUT SCHEMA
-------------
{
  "patterns_found": [
    {
      "pattern_id": "<taxonomy key, e.g. hamburger_menu>",
      "present_in": "<mobile | desktop | both>",
      "visual_evidence": "<what in the sketch implies this>",
      "confidence": "<HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW>",
      "behavior_notes": "<how it should behave based on sketch>",
      "ambiguities": "<anything unclear from sketch alone, or null>"
    }
  ],
  "applicable_criteria": ["N1", "F1", ...],
  "criteria_not_applicable": ["D2", "V1", ...],
  "implementation_priorities": {
    "mobile": ["<pattern_id in priority order for mobile viewport>"],
    "desktop": ["<pattern_id in priority order for desktop viewport>"]
  },
  "sketch_notes": "<one paragraph summarizing overall JS complexity implied
                   by these sketches and any cross-viewport differences>"
}
